00:09:18.879 --> 00:09:19.953
- That's pretty good.

00:09:19.953 --> 00:09:21.623
When I woke up this morning I was nervous

00:09:21.623 --> 00:09:23.490
about what we were gonna do all day

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:25.758
and we ended up filling it pretty well.

00:09:25.758 --> 00:09:27.656
Niki and I went outside
to read because we thought

00:09:27.656 --> 00:09:29.566
the sun was setting, it
would be nice to read

00:09:29.566 --> 00:09:31.817
and we ended up just
talking for like two hours.

00:09:31.817 --> 00:09:33.629
- Garrett and I maybe first spoke

00:09:33.629 --> 00:09:36.217
to each other like three months ago.

00:09:36.217 --> 00:09:38.406
And like, here we are telling each other

00:09:38.406 --> 00:09:41.468
what our dreams for the
future are for our lives.

00:09:41.468 --> 00:09:43.418
- I got to facetime with her fiance.

00:09:43.418 --> 00:09:44.340
Hello.

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:45.576
- [Niki's Fiance] Hi!

00:09:45.576 --> 00:09:46.494
- It's so nice to meet you.

00:09:46.494 --> 00:09:50.320
- I'm like not always the
best at meeting new people.

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:53.178
In like this one on one
setting, it's been really nice.

00:09:53.178 --> 00:09:54.348
Hey, Garrett.

00:09:54.348 --> 00:09:55.181
- Huh?

00:09:55.181 --> 00:09:56.192
- Do you wanna do sheet mask?

00:09:56.192 --> 00:09:57.352
- I've never done one before.

00:09:57.352 --> 00:09:58.888
- Yay!

00:09:58.888 --> 00:10:01.138
(laughter)

00:10:02.044 --> 00:10:03.194
- Oh, it's so goopy.

00:10:03.194 --> 00:10:04.866
Yeah, it's a little small but--

00:10:04.866 --> 00:10:07.116
(laughter)

00:10:10.889 --> 00:10:13.838
- I don't know about tiny house living.

00:10:13.838 --> 00:10:14.672
You just like--

00:10:14.672 --> 00:10:16.280
Everything you're doing is like this.

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:18.200
Cause you're like there's a person here

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:20.445
or like a wall there or like stuff here.

00:10:20.445 --> 00:10:22.150
- And that there's no privacy whatsoever.

00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:23.373
I don't know if I could actually

00:10:23.373 --> 00:10:24.996
live in this tiny house even by myself.

00:10:24.996 --> 00:10:27.195
It seems like a crazy non-starter.

00:10:27.195 --> 00:10:28.028
Oh, shit.

00:10:29.497 --> 00:10:31.425
We didn't even have like our clothes here.

00:10:31.425 --> 00:10:33.126
Like, if I had more than two
days worth of clothes here

00:10:33.126 --> 00:10:35.056
I have no idea where
I would have put them.

00:10:35.056 --> 00:10:36.142
Niki, what are you doing?

00:10:36.142 --> 00:10:39.666
- We had this like box
of lights and they were

00:10:39.666 --> 00:10:41.420
on the couch but now I can't find them.

00:10:41.420 --> 00:10:44.371
- Niki, this house is
like 180 square feet.

00:10:44.371 --> 00:10:45.204
- I know.

00:10:45.204 --> 00:10:46.648
I don't know where it went.

00:10:46.648 --> 00:10:49.248
As like a permanent,
long-term living situation

00:10:49.248 --> 00:10:51.831
I just don't think it's for me.

00:10:55.865 --> 00:10:57.333
- [In Unison] Morning.

00:10:57.333 --> 00:10:58.523
- Coffee?

00:10:58.523 --> 00:10:59.639
- Yeah, that would be great.

00:10:59.639 --> 00:11:02.249
This tiny house surpassed
some of my expectations

00:11:02.249 --> 00:11:04.273
and kind of fell short in others.

00:11:04.273 --> 00:11:06.717
Working was really inspirational.

00:11:06.717 --> 00:11:08.904
Like, you have this unbelievable view.

00:11:08.904 --> 00:11:10.775
That said, because it
was so small and cramped

00:11:10.775 --> 00:11:12.293
I had to get out of here.

00:11:12.293 --> 00:11:14.782
Like, I couldn't work on
anything for more than one hour.

00:11:14.782 --> 00:11:18.095
- It's been nice but it's too small.

00:11:18.095 --> 00:11:20.935
To tiny house livers, good on ya.

00:11:20.935 --> 00:11:22.232
I respect your lifestyle.

00:11:22.232 --> 00:11:23.467
- Bye, tiny house.

00:11:23.467 --> 00:11:24.639
- Bye, tiny house.

00:11:24.639 --> 00:11:27.222
(upbeat music)

